window.__RECONAI_SEARCH_INDEX__ = {"generatedAt":"2026-09-05T11:34:30.820Z","pages":[{"title":"Introduction","description":"ReconAI is a settlement reconciliation controller for finance ops — deterministic matching first, honest exceptions, measured accuracy.","headings":["What is ReconAI?","Who is it for?","Design pillars","Core primitives","Measured baseline","Next steps"],"text":"What is ReconAI? ReconAI is the Track 04 — AI Finance Controller build: run the books and the cash position . It closes one finance ops loop across a 50+ (we ship 81 ) labeled synthetic batch — reporting match rate, matched / partial / unresolved breakdown, and an honest exception list. See Track 04 for the full brief ↔ product ↔ tech ↔ use map. It reconciles payments, settlements, and invoices the way a finance team actually does: Match gateway, bank UTR, ERP, and GST lines through a deterministic pipeline Settle matched groups with explicit netting math (gross − fee − tax − refund + adjustment) Forecast short horizon cash from matched settlement lags Close with an honest exception list — never silent drops Deterministic matching runs first (exact → normalized → netting → fuzzy). An AI resolver is used only for residual ambiguity. Who is it for? 1. Finance ops teams closing books across gateway, bank, ERP, and tax lines 2. Razorpay merchants who need reproducible matches and a reviewable exception ledger 3. Accountants and controllers who need confidence, reason codes, and an auditable close report Design pillars Pillar What Deterministic first Reproducible matches; confidence + reason on every decision Measured accuracy Ground truth labels → match rate, precision, recall Honest exceptions Structured reason codes; zero silent drops Graceful ops Redis / OpenAI / Razorpay optional; in process fallback Every assertion (CLI, API, agent tool) flows through one audited funnel: FinanceCore . Core primitives Concept Description FinRecord Normalized finance row — source, kind, refs, amount in paise, value date MatchGroup Set of records judged to be one underlying money movement MatchType Decision label: EXACT , NORMALIZED , netted types, PARTIAL , FUZZY , AI RESOLVED , UNRESOLVED ReasonCode Why a row is unresolved: NO KEY , AMOUNT MISMATCH , PARTIAL FLAP , DATE SKEW , LOW CONFIDENCE , DUPLICATE , … CloseReport Terminal deliverable of a close run — totals, breakdown, exceptions, precision/recall FinanceCore Single audited pipeline: ingest → reconcile → judge → settle → forecast → tax → exceptions → close Measured baseline Labeled synthetic set, locked by harness tests: Metric Value Records 81 Matched 66 Partial 2 Unresolved 13 Resolved 81.48% Precision / recall 1.00 / 1.00 Next steps ~10 page product + engineering brief — identity, pipeline, stack, DB, UI, demo, bottom line. Challenge brief, why now, the bar, and how product / tech / use map to it. Run the harness batch and open the Close Cockpit in under 2 minutes. Harness, Next.js, LLM usage, Redis, Supabase, Razorpay — what is optional.","href":"/","path":"index.mdx"},{"title":"API Overview","description":"Grouped ReconAI REST endpoints for close, exceptions, agents, Razorpay, finance, control, ops, and health.","headings":["Health","Close","Exceptions","List open exceptions for a run","Agents","Razorpay","Finance","Control","Ops","Metrics (determinism dashboard)"],"text":"Base path is the Next.js app origin (local: http://localhost:3000 ). Most close/finance/control routes require an authenticated Supabase session with role owner , accountant , or viewer as noted. Interactive OpenAPI can come later — this page is the route map. Health Method Path Description GET /api/health Liveness probe — { ok, service: \"reconai\", time, checks: { redis, queue, razorpay } } (no auth) Close Method Path Description POST /api/close/upload Upload payments / settlements / invoices CSV (multipart or raw) and start a run GET /api/close/runs List close runs (newest first) POST /api/close/runs Start a daily close run (queued if REDIS URL + worker; else in process) GET /api/close/runs/[id] Run status, progress, partial metrics POST /api/close/runs/[id] Finalize — terminal step; emits CloseReport GET /api/close/runs/[id]/report Fetch the finalized close report POST /api/close/runs/[id]/post Post completed run to double entry ledger ( periodId required) POST /api/close/runs/[id]/retry Retry a failed run GET /api/close/runs/failed List failed runs POST /api/close/runs/schedule Schedule a close GET /api/close/reconcile Finance team reading of a run ( ?runId= ) — payouts, match type breakdown GET /api/close/alerts Close alerts Exceptions Method Path Description GET /api/close/exceptions Honest exception list ( ?reasonCode=&status=&runId= ) POST /api/close/exceptions/[id]/resolve Resolve / review / override (audited; never deleted) GET /api/close/exceptions/[id]/evidence Read exception evidence POST /api/close/exceptions/[id]/evidence Attach evidence Agents Method Path Description POST /api/close/agents/chat Streaming settlement Q&A ( text/plain stream; OpenAI or deterministic fallback) POST /api/close/agents/tools Direct tool invoke { name, input, runId } for harness / driver Razorpay Method Path Description GET /api/close/razorpay/sync Config status + inbox size (no secrets) POST /api/close/razorpay/sync Pull Razorpay data + flush webhook inbox into a close run POST /api/close/razorpay/payment link Create a payment link (when configured) POST /api/webhooks/razorpay Razorpay Dashboard webhook — HMAC via X Razorpay Signature Subscribed events: payment.captured , refund.processed , settlement.processed . See Razorpay Integration. Finance Method Path Description GET /api/finance/periods List fiscal periods POST /api/finance/periods Create/update period, or closePeriod / reopenPeriod GET /api/finance/ledger Query ledger entries POST /api/finance/ledger Post journal entries GET /api/finance/fx List FX rates POST /api/finance/fx Upsert FX rates GET /api/finance/metrics Aging / DSO–DPO style finance metrics POST /api/finance/gst/b2b GST B2B / GSTR 2B reconcile helper GET /api/finance/dossier/[runId]/export Export close dossier for a run Control Method Path Description POST /api/control/policy Evaluate policy engine (deterministic first gate; AI never self authorizes) POST /api/control/approvals Submit / act on approvals POST /api/control/approvals/workflow Multi step approval workflow POST /api/control/materiality Materiality threshold evaluation POST /api/control/audit/verify Verify audit chain / integrity Ops Method Path Description GET /api/ops/webhooks List outbound app webhook endpoints POST /api/ops/webhooks Register webhook ( { url, events? } ) — owner DELETE /api/ops/webhooks Remove a registered webhook App event names include close.completed , close.failed , alert , period.locked . Metrics (determinism dashboard) Method Path Description GET /api/metrics Deterministic vs AI resolved KPIs for the seeded close graph ( ?runs=a,b,c for window series) Powers /dashboard/close/metrics . No queue credentials required for the demo path.","href":"/api-reference/overview","path":"api-reference/overview.mdx"},{"title":"Authentication & roles","description":"Optional Supabase auth, app roles (owner / accountant / viewer), and safe env configuration for ReconAI.","headings":["Overview","Roles","Secrets","Supabase env vars","Best practices"],"text":"Overview Supabase Auth is optional . The local demo works without signing in — seed and in memory paths keep the close loop usable with an empty .env.local . When Supabase is configured, route guards read the acting user's role from the session and enforce write vs read access on close APIs. Roles Roles are ordered owner accountant viewer . They come from the Supabase user's app metadata.role (or user metadata.role ). Role Can do owner Full access — ingest, sync, resolve, finalize, read accountant Write capable close ops — upload, sync, sign off, read viewer Read reports and settlement Q&A; cannot ingest or sync Examples from product routes: Upload / Razorpay sync (write) → owner or accountant Settlement chat (read) → owner , accountant , or viewer If a signed in user has no role set, the app falls back to DEFAULT ROLE (default owner ) so local bootstrap stays usable. Pin DEFAULT ROLE=viewer in production for least privilege until roles are provisioned. Secrets Never expose Razorpay secrets with a NEXT PUBLIC prefix. Keep them server only: Variable Client safe? NEXT PUBLIC SUPABASE URL Yes (public anon URL) NEXT PUBLIC SUPABASE ANON KEY Yes (anon key) RAZORPAY KEY ID No — server only RAZORPAY KEY SECRET No — server only RAZORPAY WEBHOOK SECRET No — server only Supabase env vars Copy from app/.env.example : Variable Purpose If unset NEXT PUBLIC SUPABASE URL Supabase project URL Auth skipped; seed / in memory paths NEXT PUBLIC SUPABASE ANON KEY Public anon key for browser + server client Same These are the public anon credentials — safe to expose to the browser. Add DATABASE URL separately when you want Prisma → Postgres persistence. Best practices Provision real roles in app metadata for any shared or production deploy Keep Razorpay and OpenAI keys server side only Use the in memory / HeuristicJudge path for demos; add Redis and keys when you need durability and residual LLM judging","href":"/authentication","path":"authentication.mdx"},{"title":"8. Batch & Agent","description":"Locked 81-record baseline, how accuracy is measured, adversarial tests, and agent tool surface.","headings":["8.1 Batch composition","8.2 Locked audited outcomes (asserted by tests)","8.3 How accuracy is measured","8.4 Adversarial & invariant locks","9. Agent design","9.1 Philosophy","9.2 Tool surface (all route through FinanceCore)","9.3 Daily-close narrative (demo)"],"text":"8.1 Batch composition Item Detail File harness/data/batch.json ( batch 42 81 ) Seed Fixed → reproducible demo numbers Size 81 records across 4 sources Formats Mirror real Razorpay / bank / ERP / GST exports Planted cases Clean matches, pass tolerance, fee netted legs, amount mismatches, orphans ( NO KEY ), content duplicates, near misses for the judge 8.2 Locked audited outcomes (asserted by tests) 8.3 How accuracy is measured The generator emits ground truth labels ( expectedGroupKey , expectedStatus : MATCHED EXCEPTION ). CloseEngine computes precision/recall on the judged subset against those labels — match rate is measured, not assumed . 8.4 Adversarial & invariant locks Vitest suites include: close.test.ts , labels.test.ts , honesty.test.ts , semantic.test.ts adversarial.test.ts / adversarial suite.test.ts — cross match traps, fee coincidence, partial payment, duplicate, one invoice once invariant.test.ts — partition, netting identity, disjoint consumption, exception→audit, no bare fuzzy merges Plus agent, allocation, evaluation, explain, ledger, model, policy, scale, SoD tests CLI: 9. Agent design 9.1 Philosophy The agent narrates, explains, and files exceptions . It does not invent matches outside FinanceCore tools. You are the finance controller. You never guess a match — you assign confidence and file exceptions when unsure. Decisive numbers are computed by the engine, not by you. 9.2 Tool surface (all route through FinanceCore) Tool Kind Module ingestSource action IngestService runReconciliation action ReconciliationEngine judgeCandidates decision Judge (+ optional semantic) settlementQuery read SettlementService forecastWindow read CashForecaster matchTaxLine decision TaxMatcher fileException action ExceptionLedger closeRun terminal CloseEngine Hard rules: Matches / resolutions only via tools Every decision returns confidence + reason closeRun refuses to finalize with unresolved work left silent All tools emit audit events 9.3 Daily close narrative (demo) Path How Headless harness → npm run agent ( agent driver.ts ) App Streaming chat at /api/close/agents/chat + tool invocation routes Next: 9. Database.","href":"/brief/batch-and-agent","path":"brief/batch-and-agent.mdx"},{"title":"3. Closing the Books","description":"What a ReconAI close run means — the eight-stage loop and deliberate non-goals.","headings":["Settlement math identity","Out of scope (deliberate)"],"text":"A close run is one audited pass over a batch: 1. Ingest — normalize heterogeneous exports into FinRecord 2. Reconcile — exact → normalized → fee/refund/adjustment netting 3. Judge — residual flaps only ( HeuristicJudge or OpenAI residual judge) 4. Settle — bind matches to settlement batches; compute lag 5. Forecast — project 7 day cash from matched settlement lags 6. Tax — map lines to HSN/category (rules, then judge fallback) 7. Exceptions + audit — file unresolved with reason codes; append only events 8. CloseReport — totals, breakdown, unresolved lines, precision/recall Every assertion (CLI, API, agent tool) goes through FinanceCore . Settlement math identity Integer paise only — never floats: Out of scope (deliberate) Not this project Why Full double entry GL posting as the primary product Ledger helpers exist; the win is verification + close report GST filing submission to the tax portal Tax matching is in scope; e filing is not Multi tenant SaaS billing platform Control/finance APIs exist; track bar is the close loop Real bank rails / live money Razorpay test adapters + CSV/synthetic first class Adapters exist for Razorpay test mode; synthetic + CSV remain first class . Next: 4. Repository.","href":"/brief/closing-the-books","path":"brief/closing-the-books.mdx"},{"title":"9. Database & Persistence","description":"Optional Prisma/Supabase models, money as BigInt paise, and the two Redis roles.","headings":["10.1 Optional by design","set DATABASE_URL","or SQL under supabase/","10.2 Prisma models (high level)","10.3 Redis roles (two different uses)"],"text":"10.1 Optional by design The close loop works from in memory / Redis run store for demos. Prisma/Supabase persist runs for production like use. Persistence is valuable , not on the critical path for proving the math. Schema: app/prisma/schema.prisma — mirrors harness/src/core/types.ts (types are the authority). Money = signed BigInt paise. SQL also under app/supabase/migrations/ ( 0001 init.sql , 0002 seed.sql ). 10.2 Prisma models (high level) Model Purpose CloseRun One close loop; status; optional full dataset JSON snapshot FinRecord Normalized rows; unique (runId, source, sourceRef) MatchGroup / MatchLink Groups + membership + matchedOn / why Netting Full fee/refund/adjustment arithmetic Settlement Settlement legs + lag + status ForecastDatum Forward cash points TaxCategory / TaxLineMatch HSN taxonomy + line classifications Exception Honest ledger + enrichment + reviewer fields ( OPEN → REVIEWED / OVERRIDDEN / RESOLVED ) AuditEvent Append only provenance CloseReport Terminal JSON totals / breakdown / unresolved FinanceConfig Tenant tolerances / thresholds 10.3 Redis roles (two different uses) Vars Role UPSTASH REDIS REST URL / TOKEN App run store, rate limiter, cache REDIS URL (TCP / ioredis) BullMQ queue + LangGraph RedisSaver + worker Without them → in process synchronous closes. Mode When Behavior In process No REDIS URL Sync closes in the API Queued REDIS URL + npm run worker BullMQ + LangGraph checkpoints Next: 10. UI & API.","href":"/brief/database","path":"brief/database.mdx"},{"title":"12. Decisions, Demo & Bottom Line","description":"Engineering choices, phases 0–6, 2-minute demo, risks/backlog, and Track 04 bottom line.","headings":["14. Engineering decisions (why we built it this way)","15. Build history (phases 0–6)","16. Demo script (2 minutes)","17. Risks, mitigations, and backlog","Mitigated risks","Post-hackathon backlog (product-improvements.md)","18. Bottom line","Challenge checklist"],"text":"14. Engineering decisions (why we built it this way) Decision Why 1 Deterministic first, LLM last Finance needs audit trails; models hallucinate matches 2 Harness vs app split Accuracy gated without UI noise 3 Integer paise Netting identity must not float break 4 Honest exceptions over inflated match rate Wins the track bar 5 Graceful Redis / OpenAI / Razorpay Reviewers run with empty env 6 BullMQ + LangGraph only when Redis set Demo path ≠ prod fork 7 Ground truth labeled batch Measured precision/recall 8 Prisma optional Persistence ≠ proof of math 9 Razorpay as adapter Real formats without forcing live money 10 Co located dashboard screens Consistent with shared hackathon admin shell Also see Engineering Decisions. 15. Build history (phases 0–6) Phase Outcome 0 FinanceCore scaffold + Vitest + batch runner 1 81 record labeled batch + fee netting + measured metrics 2 Agent tools + residual judge + headless agent driver 3 Forecast + tax + semantic matcher 4 Close UI screens + CSV upload APIs 5 Redis / BullMQ / LangGraph worker + graceful fallback 6 Honesty drills, coverage gate, README/ops polish 16. Demo script (2 minutes) 1. npm run batch in harness/ → print real 81 / 66 / 2 / 13 / 81.48% 2. Close Cockpit → start a run; KPIs climb 3. Run Detail → match rate bars, confidence, why chip ( exact:utr , conf 0.99 ) 4. Exception List → reason codes + expected vs actual; agent files LOW CONFIDENCE live 5. Settlement Q&A + Forecast → cited answers; 7 day cash grounded in matched lags Longer walkthrough: 2 Minute Demo. 17. Risks, mitigations, and backlog Mitigated risks Risk Mitigation Cherry picked accuracy Labels + honesty tests LLM hallucination Deterministic first + thresholds in code No API key HeuristicJudge Synthetic only skepticism Real shaped formats + Razorpay adapters Post hackathon backlog ( product improvements.md ) Multi tenant isolation, server side RBAC, signed CloseReport exports, webhook idempotency ledger, real bank parsers (MT940/CAMT), fee schedules per MID, chargebacks, scheduled daily close, Slack digests, 10k+ shard uploads. See Roadmap. 18. Bottom line You did not build “an LLM that matches payments.” You built a finance ops close agent with: a tested deterministic core optional AI only on residuals a measured 81 record demo ( 81.48% resolved, P/R = 1.0 ) an explicit exception list — exactly what Track 04 asks for Stack in one breath: TypeScript harness (zero runtime deps) + Next.js 16 dashboard + Prisma/Supabase (optional) + Upstash/BullMQ/LangGraph (optional) + OpenAI residual judge (optional) + Razorpay test adapters — organized so the demo works with empty env and the math stays reproducible under CI. That is Track 04 answered completely: throughput + measured accuracy + an honest exception list. Challenge checklist Requirement Covered? 50+ synthetic records Yes — 81 labeled, 4 sources One closed finance ops loop Yes — ingest → close report Report match rate Yes — CLI + UI + CloseReport Exceptions it could not resolve Yes — structured reason codes Multi source reconciliation Yes Settlement Q&A Yes Forward cash forecast Yes Tax line matcher Yes Throughput + measured accuracy + honesty Yes — tests lock baseline Back to 1. Executive Summary · short map: Track 04.","href":"/brief/decisions-demo","path":"brief/decisions-demo.mdx"},{"title":"6. Domain Model & Money","description":"Canonical types, FinRecord, FinanceConfig tolerances, and the P0 settlement netting identity.","headings":["6.1 Canonical types (harness/src/core/types.ts)","Sources (SourceKind)","Record kinds (RecordKind)","Match types (MatchType)","Exception reason codes (ReasonCode)","6.2 FinRecord (normalized row)","6.3 Finance tolerances (FinanceConfig defaults)","6.4 Settlement netting identity (P0 review rule)"],"text":"6.1 Canonical types ( harness/src/core/types.ts ) Types are the single source of truth . Prisma enums/models mirror them; the app must not redefine them. Sources ( SourceKind ) razorpay gateway bank utr erp orders gst invoices Record kinds ( RecordKind ) PAYMENT · SETTLEMENT · REFUND · FEE · INVOICE · CHARGEBACK · ADJUSTMENT Match types ( MatchType ) EXACT · NORMALIZED · FEE NETTED · REFUND NETTED · ADJUSTMENT NETTED · PARTIAL · FUZZY · AI RESOLVED · UNRESOLVED Exception reason codes ( ReasonCode ) NO KEY · AMOUNT MISMATCH · PARTIAL FLAP · DATE SKEW · LOW CONFIDENCE · DUPLICATE · UNKNOWN SOURCE 6.2 FinRecord (normalized row) Every raw export becomes a FinRecord with: Field Role source + sourceRef Idempotency key within a run amountPaise Signed (+ inflow, − outflow) Cross keys utr , gatewayRef ( pay … ), orderRef ( ORD … ) feeTaxPaise Optional on FEE rows (GST on gateway fee) raw Original row preserved verbatim 6.3 Finance tolerances ( FinanceConfig defaults) Rule Default Meaning paiseTolerance 50 ≤ ₹0.50 difference allowed (fee/rounding) dateWindowDays 1 Value dates within 1 day resolveThreshold 0.7 Min judge confidence to resolve residual exactThreshold 1.0 Hard key equality normalizedThreshold 0.95 Post normalization key equality maxExceptionAge 5 Flag stale open exceptions for humans 6.4 Settlement netting identity (P0 review rule) Netting never guesses a fee. It only fires when FEE / REFUND / ADJUSTMENT records are actually present and the arithmetic balances within tolerance. Groups carry a full NettingBreakdown : Field Role grossPaise Base payment / invoice amount (abs) feePaise Gateway FEE records (abs) taxOnFeePaise Tax on those fees ( FEE.feeTaxPaise , abs) refundPaise REFUND records (abs) adjustmentPaise ADJUSTMENT records (signed) netExpectedPaise gross − fee − taxOnFee − refund + adjustment actualSettlementPaise Settlement / bank UTR legs (abs) variancePaise actualSettlement − netExpected Next: 7. FinanceCore.","href":"/brief/domain-model","path":"brief/domain-model.mdx"},{"title":"7. FinanceCore Pipeline","description":"Module-by-module close funnel — ingest through close, plus the control plane.","headings":["7.1 Ingest (ingest.ts)","7.2 Reconcile (reconcile.ts)","7.3 Judge (judge.ts + semantic.ts)","7.4 Settle (settle.ts)","7.5 Forecast (forecast.ts)","7.6 Tax (tax.ts)","7.7 Exceptions (exception.ts) + Audit (audit.ts)","7.8 Close (close.ts)","7.9 Control plane (harness/src/control/)"],"text":"Every CLI command, API route, and agent tool assertion flows through this funnel. 7.1 Ingest ( ingest.ts ) Normalizes gateway / bank / ERP / GST rows into FinRecord Idempotent on (source, sourceRef) Duplicate source refs → DUPLICATE exceptions Also detects content duplicates (same source/amount/date/counterparty even if refs differ) 7.2 Reconcile ( reconcile.ts ) Ordered deterministic passes: 1. Exact keys — union find over utr: / gateway: / order: / invoice keys → confidence ~1.0 (or 0.98 if amounts differ within tolerance) 2. Normalized keys — case/space/punctuation strip + leading zero collapse ( UTR00123 → UTR123 ) → confidence 0.95 3. Netting — amount disagreement explained by fee/refund/adjustment math → FEE NETTED / REFUND NETTED / ADJUSTMENT NETTED @ 0.98 4. Conflicts / flaps — beyond tolerance and unexplained → conflicted set or residual for the judge; never a silent fake match 7.3 Judge ( judge.ts + semantic.ts ) Mode Behavior Default HeuristicJudge Fully reproducible, no API key Optional OpenAI residual judge Ambiguous candidates → may emit AI RESOLVED Optional semantic boost (residual only) NgramSemanticMatcher (offline default) or EmbeddingSemanticMatcher (OpenAI when keyed) Below resolveThreshold → PARTIAL / UNRESOLVED + exception — never guessed “done”. 7.4 Settle ( settle.ts ) Binds matched groups to settlement batches Computes settlement lag vs value date Exposes a queryable ledger for Settlement Q&A 7.5 Forecast ( forecast.ts ) Projects next day / 7 day cash from matched inflows/outflows and historical lag distribution Confidence band grounded in matched lags ( reconciledIn flag) 7.6 Tax ( tax.ts ) Rule based HSN / category map first Judge fallback for ambiguous descriptions Output: category + confidence + RULE JUDGED 7.7 Exceptions ( exception.ts ) + Audit ( audit.ts ) Every unresolved record → ExceptionRecord with reason code, rationale, candidates, expected/actual/variance enrichment Append only AuditEvent s ( INGEST / MATCH / JUDGE / SETTLE / FORECAST / TAX / EXCEPTION / CLOSE ) Exception list integrity is tested — empty because hidden fails the bar 7.8 Close ( close.ts ) CloseEngine.run(batch) orchestrates the full loop and emits CloseReport : Totals + per source stats Explicit breakdown: { records, matched, partial, unresolved, matchRate } UnresolvedLine[] (expected vs actual vs reason vs confidence) Precision / recall vs ground truth labels Confidence bins, audit count, judge metadata Also wires supporting pieces: double entry ledger helpers, allocation solver, optional compiled DSL rules. 7.9 Control plane ( harness/src/control/ ) Beyond core matching: Capability Role Policy Configurable finance rules Materiality Critical exceptions (e.g. large AMOUNT MISMATCH , duplicates) SoD Resolver ≠ approver on critical items Approval workflow Pending / approved / rejected Audit chain Verify integrity of the event trail Next: 8. Batch & Agent.","href":"/brief/financecore","path":"brief/financecore.mdx"},{"title":"11. Ops & Deploy","description":"Local run commands, environment variables, Vercel setup, and GitHub Actions CI.","headings":["13.1 Local","Engine (empty env is fine)","Dashboard","optional durable worker:","13.2 Environment variables","13.3 Vercel","13.4 CI"],"text":"13.1 Local 13.2 Environment variables Variable Needed for If unset Supabase URL / anon key Auth + persisted app data Seed / in memory DATABASE URL Prisma Postgres Skip DB Upstash REST URL/token Run store, rate limit No ops REDIS URL BullMQ + LangGraph + worker In process closes OPENAI API KEY Residual LLM, chat, embeddings HeuristicJudge + n gram Razorpay key/secret/webhook Live test sync + webhooks CSV / 81 record batch CLOSE ORG ID / GSTIN / display name Demo merchant branding Defaults (e.g. Rhae) Never prefix Razorpay secrets with NEXT PUBLIC . 13.3 Vercel 1. Import the ReconAI repo 2. Root Directory: app 3. Include files outside root so file:../harness resolves 4. Set env vars; deploy 5. Webhook: https:// /api/webhooks/razorpay See Deployment for the full checklist. 13.4 CI GitHub Actions roughly: 1. harness — install + test 2. app — install, lint, typecheck, unit tests, ops verify, production build Next: 12. Decisions & Demo.","href":"/brief/ops-and-deploy","path":"brief/ops-and-deploy.mdx"},{"title":"1. Executive Summary","description":"ReconAI full project brief — product identity, track bar, and one-sentence definition.","headings":["ReconAI — Full Project Brief","Product identity","One sentence","The track bar","Why it exists (the bar)","Locked audited baseline (tests enforce this)","Continue reading"],"text":"ReconAI — Full Project Brief Track 04 · AI Finance Controller · Run the books and the cash position This Full Brief is the long form product + engineering document (≈10 pages). Use the sidebar under Full Brief for the rest of the sections. Product identity Field Value Product name ReconAI (Settlement Reconciliation Controller) Hackathon track AI Finance Controller — run the books and the cash position Repo github.com/Rhae Shane/ReconAI Local folder AI Finance Controller/ License MIT © 2026 Rhae Shane / ReconAI Default branch main Demo batch 81 records · 4 sources · 81.48% resolved · precision/recall = 1.00 Build status Phases 0–6 complete (engine → agent → UI → Redis/LangGraph → hardening) One sentence An agent that takes a messy multi source finance batch (≥50 records; ours is 81 ), reconciles it across gateway / bank / ERP / GST, settles, forecasts cash, maps tax, and ships a Close Report with match rate + precision/recall + an honest exception list — nothing silently dropped. The track bar Throughput plus measured accuracy plus an honest exception list. One cherry picked match proves nothing. ReconAI was designed so that bar is engineered in , not bolted on: deterministic matching first, LLM only on residual ambiguity, ground truth labels for precision/recall, and every unresolved row filed with a structured reason code — never silently dropped. Why it exists (the bar) The track’s “why now” is: verification, not generation , is the bottleneck. Reconciliation / settlement / forecasting are still manual. Deliverable How you prove it Throughput Full 81 record close in well under a second; scalable via BullMQ Measured accuracy Ground truth labels → match rate, precision, recall Honest exceptions Every unresolved row gets a reason code + rationale Locked audited baseline (tests enforce this) Continue reading Page Contents 2. Why It Exists Why now, track directions, design thesis 3. Closing the Books What a close run means / non goals 4. Repository Layout + harness vs app split 5. Tech Stack Full stack + graceful degradation 6. Domain Model Types, FinRecord, tolerances, netting 7. FinanceCore Module by module pipeline 8. Batch & Agent Synthetic batch, tools, daily close narrative 9. Database Prisma models, Redis roles 10. UI & API Screens + selected routes 11. Ops & Deploy Local, env, Vercel, CI 12. Decisions & Demo Phases, demo script, risks, bottom line","href":"/brief/overview","path":"brief/overview.mdx"},{"title":"4. Repository Architecture","description":"Repo layout, harness vs app split, and why accuracy-critical math is package-isolated.","headings":["4.1 Why two packages?"],"text":"Local checkout folder name may be AI Finance Controller/ ; GitHub repo is ReconAI . 4.1 Why two packages? Package Role harness/ ( controller harness ) Accuracy critical math; Vitest without Next/Prisma/React app/ ( reconai ) Thin dashboard + APIs + ops; imports file:../harness Split on purpose: accuracy critical math lives in harness/ so Vitest can gate it without Next/Prisma/React. The app is a thin UI/API shell. Dashboard churn cannot silently break settlement math. CI gates the engine independently. Next: 5. Tech Stack.","href":"/brief/repository","path":"brief/repository.mdx"},{"title":"5. Tech Stack","description":"Full stack table — core, Next.js, AI, LangGraph, BullMQ, Supabase, Razorpay, tests, docs, deploy.","headings":["Where the LLM is used","Graceful degradation"],"text":"Layer Choice Why Core engine Pure TypeScript, zero runtime deps Headless, CI friendly, reproducible App framework Next.js 16 App Router, React 19, TS strict Server Components + co located components/ UI shadcn/ui, Tailwind v4, Lucide, Recharts, TanStack Table, Zustand, Sonner, Vaul, cmdk Shared admin shell patterns AI Vercel AI SDK ( ai ) + OpenAI ( @ai sdk/openai ) Residual judge, settlement chat, embeddings Agent graph LangGraph StateGraph + optional RedisSaver Durable multi step close when Redis is on Queue BullMQ + ioredis ( REDIS URL ) Queued close runs + horizontal workers App Redis Upstash REST ( @upstash/redis ) Run store, rate limit, cache DB Prisma 7 + Postgres (Supabase) Optional persistence; mirrors harness types Auth Supabase Auth ( @supabase/ssr ) Roles for cockpit / exception resolve Payments Razorpay test keys + HMAC webhooks Live sync optional; CSV/synthetic first class Money Signed integer paise (BigInt in DB) No float rounding in netting Lint / format Biome + Husky Fast checks Tests Vitest (harness + app), Playwright smoke, coverage gate Accuracy locked by tests Docs Mintlify ( docs/ ) Get Started / Concepts / Close Loop / Full Brief / API Deploy Vercel ( app/ root) + optional long lived worker host Zero infra demo path Where the LLM is used Path Uses LLM? Notes Exact / normalized / netting No Pure rules + paise identity Residual without OPENAI API KEY No HeuristicJudge + n gram Residual with key Yes OpenAI residual judge → may emit AI RESOLVED Settlement Q&A Yes (optional) Streamed citations; deterministic fallback Tax residual descriptions Maybe Rules first; judge fallback Fee / tax / settlement amounts Never Always from records via FinanceCore Match rate / P/R Never Labels + engine outcomes Philosophy: LLM everywhere is the trap. The model arbitrates residual ambiguity and narrates; it does not fudge numbers. Graceful degradation Empty .env.local still runs the demo — HeuristicJudge , in memory/in process close, no Redis required. Variable Enables Without it OPENAI API KEY Residual LLM, chat, embeddings HeuristicJudge + n gram REDIS URL BullMQ + LangGraph checkpoints In process close Upstash REST Run store, rate limit No ops / memory Supabase / DATABASE URL Auth + Postgres Seed / in memory Razorpay keys Sync + webhooks CSV + 81 record batch Next: 6. Domain Model.","href":"/brief/tech-stack","path":"brief/tech-stack.mdx"},{"title":"10. UI & API","description":"Close Cockpit screens, demo flow, selected API routes, and LangGraph node order.","headings":["11. Application UI map","Demo flow (UI)","12. API surface (selected)","Control / finance","Extra surface beyond the core loop","LangGraph node order (when queued)"],"text":"11. Application UI map Built on the Next.js admin shell ( AGENTS.md co location: page + components/ + sidebar). Screen Route What you see Close Cockpit /dashboard/close Runs list, KPIs, start run, CSV upload, Razorpay sync card Run Detail /dashboard/close/[runId] Match rate bars, confidence distribution, reconciliation grid, why chips Exceptions /dashboard/close/exceptions Reason codes, rationale, resolve/override drawer Settlement Q&A /dashboard/close/settlement Chat over settled ledger with citations Forecast /dashboard/close/forecast 7 day cash band grounded in matched lags Tax /dashboard/close/tax HSN/category matches + confidence Plus billing, metrics, trust, diff Ops / trust / run to run comparison Landing/marketing lives under app/(external) with a branded landing experience. Demo flow (UI) Start run → KPIs climb → match rate bars / confidence / why chips ( exact:utr , conf 0.99 ) → exception list with reason codes → settlement Q&A + 7 day cash forecast. 12. API surface (selected) Route Purpose POST /api/close/runs Start close (sync or enqueue BullMQ) GET /api/close/runs/:id Status + progress + metrics POST /api/close/runs/:id Finalize → terminal CloseReport GET /api/close/runs/:id/report Fetch / download report POST /api/close/upload CSV upload (≤10 MiB, rate limited) → { runId, report } GET /api/close/exceptions Filterable exception list POST /api/close/exceptions/:id/resolve Accountant resolve/override (audited) POST /api/close/agents/chat Streaming settlement Q&A POST /api/close/agents/tools Direct tool invocation POST /api/close/razorpay/sync Pull Razorpay test data POST /api/webhooks/razorpay HMAC: payment.captured , refund.processed , settlement.processed GET /api/health { service: \"reconai\", … } Control / finance /api/control/ , /api/finance/ — policy, approvals, audit verify, GST, ledger, FX, metrics, dossier export. Extra surface beyond the core loop Control plane: approvals, SoD, materiality, policy, audit chain verify Finance APIs: dossier, FX, GST, ledger, metrics Razorpay: sync, payment links, webhooks CSV upload for real format batches without live money LangGraph node order (when queued) Full route map: API Overview. Next: 11. Ops & Deploy.","href":"/brief/ui-and-api","path":"brief/ui-and-api.mdx"},{"title":"2. Why It Exists","description":"Track why-now, all four example directions mapped to product surfaces, and the deterministic-first thesis.","headings":["2.1 The 2026 “why now”","2.2 Example directions from the track (all covered)","2.3 Design thesis in one line","Why this wins for judges","Data sources (4)","Match types & reason codes (quick reference)"],"text":"2.1 The 2026 “why now” Payment generation is fast. Verification is still slow. Merchants and finance teams still reconcile by hand across: Gateway captures (Razorpay payments, fees, refunds) Bank statement lines (UTR) ERP / order systems GST invoices / HSN lines That gap — matching one money movement across four systems — is exactly agent + data work, and it is where trust matters more than clever text generation. 2.2 Example directions from the track (all covered) Direction Where it lives in ReconAI Multi source reconciliation ReconciliationEngine + Close Cockpit / Run Detail Settlement Q&A agent Settlement screen + POST /api/close/agents/chat Forward cash forecaster CashForecaster + /dashboard/close/forecast Tax line matcher TaxMatcher + /dashboard/close/tax ReconAI does not pick one direction — it closes all four inside one finance ops loop. 2.3 Design thesis in one line Deterministic first, LLM last. Rules make reproducible matches; the model only judges what rules cannot; anything below threshold becomes a visible exception. Why this wins for judges 1. Exact “why now” — verification bottleneck, not another chat UI. 2. The bar is engineered in — measured metrics + honesty tests. 3. Full loop — raw batch → Close Report, not a single toy match. 4. Trustworthy — LLM never invents settlement math; FinanceCore is the chokepoint. Data sources (4) Source Role Cross keys razorpay gateway Payments, fees, refunds pay … , UTR bank utr Bank statement lines UTR erp orders ERP orders ORD … , gateway ref gst invoices GST invoices order ref Synthetic batch: harness/data/batch.json ( batch 42 81 ), fixed seed, labeled for precision/recall. Match types & reason codes (quick reference) Match types: EXACT , NORMALIZED , FEE NETTED , REFUND NETTED , ADJUSTMENT NETTED , PARTIAL , FUZZY , AI RESOLVED , UNRESOLVED . Exception reason codes: NO KEY , AMOUNT MISMATCH , PARTIAL FLAP , DATE SKEW , LOW CONFIDENCE , DUPLICATE (plus UNKNOWN SOURCE ). Next: 3. Closing the Books.","href":"/brief/why-it-exists","path":"brief/why-it-exists.mdx"},{"title":"Close Loop Overview","description":"Close Cockpit UI routes — runs, exceptions, settlement Q&A, forecast, tax, metrics, and trust.","headings":["UI map","Close Cockpit (/dashboard/close)","Run Detail (/dashboard/close/[runId])","Exceptions (/dashboard/close/exceptions)","Settlement, Forecast, Tax","Metrics & Trust","Related APIs"],"text":"The Close Cockpit is the operator surface for ReconAI’s monthly close loop: reconcile, settle, forecast, tax match, and file honest exceptions. All screens live under /dashboard/close . UI map Screen Route Purpose Close Cockpit /dashboard/close Start runs, upload CSV, Razorpay sync, schedule, run list + KPIs Run Detail /dashboard/close/[runId] Match rate bars, confidence, reconciliation grid, why chips, progress Exceptions /dashboard/close/exceptions Reason coded residual list; resolve / override with audit Settlement Q&A /dashboard/close/settlement Cited chat over settled ledger + aging / journal periods Forecast /dashboard/close/forecast 7 day cash band from settlement lag distribution Tax /dashboard/close/tax GST / ITC match views and tax match table Metrics /dashboard/close/metrics Deterministic vs AI resolved health over demo runs Trust /dashboard/close/trust Measured trust board — matched / partial / human review stay visible Close Cockpit ( /dashboard/close ) Entry point for the loop: Start run — POST /api/close/runs (in process or BullMQ when Redis + worker are up) Upload — drop payments / settlements / invoices CSV Razorpay sync — pull test mode data and flush webhook inbox Schedule / failed runs — recurring close + recovery panels Trust strip — quick honesty signal before diving into a run Run Detail ( /dashboard/close/[runId] ) Deep dive on one close: Determinism KPIs and confidence distribution Reconciliation grid with match method (e.g. exact:utr ) Trace / progress while the graph is running Finalize emits the CloseReport via POST /api/close/runs/[id] Exceptions ( /dashboard/close/exceptions ) Honest residual queue. Every line has a reason code ( NO KEY , AMOUNT MISMATCH , PARTIAL FLAP , DATE SKEW , LOW CONFIDENCE , DUPLICATE ) and rationale. Resolutions are audited; exceptions are never deleted. Settlement, Forecast, Tax Route What you show /dashboard/close/settlement Ask questions; answers cite matched records /dashboard/close/forecast Next 7 days projected from matched settlement lags /dashboard/close/tax Invoice ↔ GSTR 2B style matching and ITC summary Metrics & Trust Route What you show /dashboard/close/metrics How much volume cleared without an LLM call ( /api/metrics ) /dashboard/close/trust Measured outcomes board — nothing cherry picked Related APIs Close, exceptions, agents, and Razorpay routes that back these screens are listed in the API Overview. For a walkthrough narrative, see the 2 Minute Demo.","href":"/close-loop/overview","path":"close-loop/overview.mdx"},{"title":"Exceptions","description":"Honest ReasonCode ledger, UnresolvedLine expected vs actual, and resolve via API or UI.","headings":["ReasonCode","Honest Exception List","UnresolvedLine","Resolve Via API Or UI"],"text":"Unresolved work is never silently dropped. Every leftover record gets a structured ReasonCode , a human rationale, and (when known) an expected vs actual paise split. That list is the trust surface of a close — not an afterthought. Core types: ExceptionRecord , UnresolvedLine , ReasonCode in harness/src/core/types.ts . Store: ExceptionLedger in harness/src/core/exception.ts . ReasonCode ReasonCode Meaning NO KEY No usable reference key (orphan / no cross source join) AMOUNT MISMATCH Key matches but amounts differ beyond tolerance (and netting did not explain it) PARTIAL FLAP Some signals matched, not enough to resolve DATE SKEW Amount matched but value date outside the configured window LOW CONFIDENCE Judge could not reach resolveThreshold DUPLICATE Idempotency collision on (source, sourceRef) or content duplicate hygiene hit UNKNOWN SOURCE Unrecognised SourceKind Exceptions also carry optional enrichment: matchType , confidence , expectedPaise / actualPaise / variancePaise , fee/refund/adjustment components, and optional aiReasoning . Honest Exception List Principles: Append only — records are never deleted; status moves instead. Always coded — every unresolved item has a ReasonCode + rationale. Visible on close — CloseReport.exceptions and unresolved[] still surface open items after the close control finalizes. Integrity over vanity — empty because hidden fails the product bar. Statuses on ExceptionRecord : OPEN → REVIEWED OVERRIDDEN RESOLVED . UnresolvedLine The close report breaks each unresolved record the way a finance team reads it: Field Meaning recordId Record being reconciled (invoice / payment / gateway, etc.) ref Human key (e.g. INV 1234 , pay 19 ) expectedPaise What we expected (invoice / payment amount) actualPaise Settlement (or best near match) actually present differencePaise expected − actual (positive = shortfall) reason ReasonCode for why it did not resolve cleanly confidence Resolver confidence in the diagnosis (0..1) status NEEDS REVIEW or RESOLVED Resolve Via API Or UI Accountants resolve without deleting history. Surface Path List / filter GET /api/close/exceptions?reasonCode=&status=&runId= Resolve / override POST /api/close/exceptions/:id/resolve Evidence GET / POST /api/close/exceptions/:id/evidence UI /dashboard/close/exceptions Resolve body: Allowed statuses: REVIEWED , OVERRIDDEN , RESOLVED . Each change is audited. Role gate: owner / accountant.","href":"/concepts/exceptions","path":"concepts/exceptions.mdx"},{"title":"FinanceCore","description":"The audited chokepoint: harness modules, shared types, and HeuristicJudge vs OpenAI residual judge.","headings":["Why A Chokepoint","Modules","Types Owned By The Harness","HeuristicJudge Vs OpenAI"],"text":"FinanceCore is the single audited funnel for ReconAI. CLI batch runs, HTTP APIs, and agent tools all route engine work through it — the model (when present) narrates on top of engine computed numbers; it does not invent settlement math. In code, the orchestrator is CloseEngine in harness/src/core/close.ts , composing the modules under harness/src/core/ . The Next.js app imports that harness and optionally wraps the same stages in LangGraph ( src/lib/close/graph.ts ). Why A Chokepoint Concern How FinanceCore handles it Reproducibility Deterministic ingest → reconcile → netting before any LLM Auditability AuditEngine events on every stage action Honesty ExceptionLedger + CloseReport.unresolved never hide leftovers Separation Framework free harness; UI/ops stay thin Modules Module File Role IngestService ingest.ts Normalize rows → FinRecord ; duplicate detection ReconciliationEngine reconcile.ts Exact / normalized / netting match groups + flaps Judge ( HeuristicJudge ) judge.ts Residual arbitration interface + default implementation SemanticMatcher semantic.ts Optional n gram or embedding similarity for residuals SettlementService settle.ts Bind groups to settlements; lag stats; settle Q&A CashForecaster forecast.ts Cash projection from matched lag distribution TaxMatcher tax.ts Rule based HSN/category match + judge fallback AuditEngine audit.ts Append only stage audit events ExceptionLedger exception.ts Append only honest exceptions CloseEngine close.ts Runs the full loop → CloseReport Supporting pieces in the same tree include config.ts (tolerances / thresholds), ledger.ts (double entry journal for netted groups), and types.ts (authoritative shapes). Types Owned By The Harness harness/src/core/types.ts is the source of truth. The app mirrors these for API/UI; Prisma (optional) mirrors them for persistence. Important exports include: Identity & money: SourceKind , RecordKind , FinRecord Matching: MatchType , MatchMethod , MatchGroup , MatchLink , NettingBreakdown Exceptions & close: ReasonCode , ExceptionRecord , UnresolvedLine , MatchBreakdown , CloseReport Downstream: Settlement , ForecastDatum , TaxLineMatch , AuditEvent , FinanceConfig Residual I/O: Candidate , JudgeResult All amounts are signed integer paise . HeuristicJudge Vs OpenAI Mode When Behavior HeuristicJudge Default / no API key Deterministic residual scoring → FUZZY or a reason code OpenAI residual judge OPENAI API KEY set App ClaudeJudge ( claude judge.ts ) uses OpenAI chat + embeddings → can emit AI RESOLVED Rules of the residual path: Only flaps after deterministic matching reach the judge. Confidence below resolveThreshold → exception ( LOW CONFIDENCE / PARTIAL FLAP , etc.), not a forced match. Without OPENAI API KEY , the audited batch and local demo stay green on HeuristicJudge + n gram semantic fallback. With the key, embeddings can enrich candidacy text; amounts still come from the engine. Agent tools follow the same rule: every tool routes through FinanceCore; the LLM does not compute gross / fee / settlement legs.","href":"/concepts/financecore","path":"concepts/financecore.mdx"},{"title":"How It Works","description":"ReconAI close pipeline from ingest through honest close, and how it runs in-process or queued.","headings":["Pipeline","Where The Code Lives","Run Modes","Recommended Mental Model"],"text":"ReconAI matches gateway, bank UTR, ERP, and GST lines into one audited close. Every assertion (CLI, API, agent tool) flows through the same funnel in harness/src/core/ , orchestrated by CloseEngine and optionally by the LangGraph close graph in the app. Currency is integer paise (signed). Shared shapes live in harness/src/core/types.ts . Pipeline Stage Module What happens Ingest IngestService Normalize raw rows → FinRecord ; idempotent on source + sourceRef Reconcile ReconciliationEngine Exact → normalized → fee/refund/adjustment netting → residual flaps Judge HeuristicJudge / residual LLM Arbitrate flaps only; file ReasonCode when confidence is low Settle SettlementService Bind match groups to settlement batches; lag stats; Q&A ledger Forecast CashForecaster Project cash from matched settlement lag distribution Tax TaxMatcher HSN/category rules, with judge fallback for residual lines Exceptions ExceptionLedger Append only honest list — never silent drops Close CloseEngine / graph closeRun Emit CloseReport with MatchBreakdown + per record UnresolvedLine[] Audit events are recorded along the way ( AuditEngine ). The close control does not hide open exceptions: the report still surfaces every unresolved line. Where The Code Lives Layer Path Role Core engine harness/src/core/ Framework free TypeScript; settlement math and matching Close orchestrator harness/src/core/close.ts CloseEngine.run(batch) wires the pipeline above LangGraph workflow app/src/lib/close/graph.ts Stage order, revision loop, checkpointed close Ops queue app/src/lib/ops/queue.ts BullMQ close runs when Redis is configured The graph nodes are a workflow over engine computed data — they do not re derive amounts: closeRun is terminal: it finalizes only when exceptions are clear, or after MAX REVISIONS passes (still with every open exception visible). Run Modes Mode Trigger Behavior In process No REDIS URL POST /api/close/runs runs the close synchronously in the API process Queued REDIS URL set + npm run worker BullMQ enqueues close run jobs; worker runs LangGraph + optional RedisSaver Without Redis, the default checkpointer is in memory ( MemorySaver ). With a TCP REDIS URL that supports RediSearch, the graph can use RedisSaver for durable checkpoints. Upstash REST vars for the run store/rate limiter are independent of the worker TCP URL. Recommended Mental Model 1. Ingest and normalize every source into FinRecord . 2. Resolve as much as possible with deterministic keys and settlement identity. 3. Send only residual flaps to the judge. 4. Settle, forecast, and tax map from matched groups. 5. File every leftover as an exception with a reason code. 6. Close with a report that shows matched / partial / unresolved honestly.","href":"/concepts/how-it-works","path":"concepts/how-it-works.mdx"},{"title":"Matching","description":"Deterministic-first MatchType labels, settlement identity in paise, and residual judgment.","headings":["MatchType","Settlement Identity","Deterministic First, Judge Last","What Matching Does Not Do"],"text":"Every reconciliation decision carries an explicit MatchType . Finance teams read that label as “what we actually did with these records.” Matching is deterministic first : keys and settlement math run before any residual judge. Types are defined in harness/src/core/types.ts . The engine that applies them is ReconciliationEngine in harness/src/core/reconcile.ts . MatchType MatchType Meaning EXACT Same primary key (e.g. UTR / gateway ref) and amount within exact threshold NORMALIZED Normalized reference key match within normalized threshold / tolerance FEE NETTED Settlement identity holds with gateway fee legs present REFUND NETTED Identity holds with refund legs driving the net ADJUSTMENT NETTED Identity holds with adjustment legs present PARTIAL Some signals matched — not enough to resolve → usually PARTIAL FLAP FUZZY Residual resolved by HeuristicJudge (reproducible, no model) AI RESOLVED Residual resolved by the OpenAI backed residual judge UNRESOLVED Filed to the exception ledger with a ReasonCode MatchMethod ( EXACT NORMALIZED JUDGED NETTED ) describes how the group was formed; MatchType is the explainable decision label on the group and each MatchLink . Settlement Identity Netted matches must satisfy the P0 identity in integer paise (never floats): Captured on NettingBreakdown : Field Role grossPaise Base payment / invoice amount (abs) feePaise Gateway FEE records (abs) taxOnFeePaise Tax on those fees ( FEE.feeTaxPaise , abs) refundPaise REFUND records (abs) adjustmentPaise ADJUSTMENT records (signed) netExpectedPaise gross − fee − taxOnFee − refund + adjustment actualSettlementPaise Settlement / bank UTR legs (abs) variancePaise actualSettlement − netExpected (≈ 0 when balanced) Nothing is guessed: a component only nets when it actually contains the driving FEE / REFUND / ADJUSTMENT records and the identity balances within paiseTolerance . Otherwise it stays an amount conflict ( AMOUNT MISMATCH ), not a silent merge. Deterministic First, Judge Last Order of operations: 1. Compiled rules (optional) → exact key groups → normalized key groups. 2. Netting for components whose raw amounts disagree but settlement math explains the gap ( FEE NETTED / REFUND NETTED / ADJUSTMENT NETTED ). 3. Residual flaps → candidates for the judge. 4. Judge assigns FUZZY or AI RESOLVED , or files an exception ( UNRESOLVED + reason code). Optional semantic signal ( SemanticMatcher in harness/src/core/semantic.ts ) can enrich residual scoring. Default is n gram; OpenAI embeddings are opt in when OPENAI API KEY is set. Semantic matching never invents a primary key match ahead of the deterministic passes. What Matching Does Not Do Inflate match rate by dropping hard cases. Use floating point money. Let the LLM invent fee, tax, or settlement amounts — those come from records already on the group.","href":"/concepts/matching","path":"concepts/matching.mdx"},{"title":"Architecture","description":"System shape, FinanceCore pipeline, ops modes, UI map, and measured baseline for ReconAI.","headings":["System shape","FinanceCore pipeline","Matching model","Ops modes","UI map","Measured baseline (locked by harness tests)"],"text":"Settlement reconciliation controller: match gateway, bank UTR, ERP, and GST lines; settle; forecast; tax map; close with an honest exception list. System shape Layer Path Role Core engine harness/src/core/ Framework free TypeScript; zero runtime deps CLI / bench harness/src/cli/ batch , gen batch , agent , bench App UI + API app/ Thin Next.js surface over the harness Ops src/lib/ops/ , src/worker/ Redis, BullMQ, rate limit, durable worker FinanceCore pipeline Every assertion (CLI, API, agent tool) flows through one funnel: 1. Ingest — normalize rows → FinRecord (idempotent by source + sourceRef ) 2. Reconcile — EXACT → NORMALIZED → fee/refund/adjustment netting → residual flaps 3. Judge — HeuristicJudge by default; optional OpenAI residual judge + semantic matcher 4. Settle — bind matches to settlement batches; lag stats; Q&A ledger 5. Forecast + tax — cash projection from lags; HSN/category rules (+ judge fallback) 6. Exceptions + audit — structured reason codes; append only events; never silent drops 7. Close — CloseReport with breakdown + per record unresolved lines Currency is integer paise (signed). Types in harness/src/core/types.ts are authoritative; Prisma mirrors them for optional Postgres persistence. Matching model Match type Meaning EXACT / NORMALIZED Deterministic key / normalized key FEE NETTED / REFUND NETTED / ADJUSTMENT NETTED Settlement math identity holds PARTIAL Some signals matched → PARTIAL FLAP FUZZY / AI RESOLVED Residual only UNRESOLVED Exception with reason code Reason codes include NO KEY , AMOUNT MISMATCH , PARTIAL FLAP , DATE SKEW , LOW CONFIDENCE , DUPLICATE . Ops modes Mode Trigger Behavior In process No REDIS URL POST /api/close/runs runs synchronously Queued REDIS URL set + npm run worker BullMQ close runs + LangGraph + RedisSaver Upstash REST vars power the app run store and rate limiter independently of the TCP worker URL. UI map Screen Route Close Cockpit /dashboard/close Run Detail /dashboard/close/[runId] Exceptions /dashboard/close/exceptions Settlement Q&A /dashboard/close/settlement Forecast /dashboard/close/forecast Tax /dashboard/close/tax Measured baseline (locked by harness tests) See SPEC.md for the full product/architecture planning artifact and BUILD PLAN.md for phase gates.","href":"/engineering/architecture","path":"engineering/architecture.mdx"},{"title":"Engineering Decisions","description":"Non-obvious choices in ReconAI and why they stick.","headings":["1. Deterministic-first, LLM last","2. Split harness/ from the Next.js app","3. Integer paise, never floats","4. Honest exceptions over inflated match rate","5. Graceful degradation for Redis / OpenAI / Razorpay","6. BullMQ + LangGraph only when REDIS_URL is set","7. Ground-truth labeled synthetic batch","8. Prisma / Supabase optional","9. Razorpay test mode + webhooks as adapters","10. Co-located dashboard screens"],"text":"Short record of non obvious choices and why they stick. 1. Deterministic first, LLM last Decision: Exact → normalized → netting → optional semantic → LLM residual only. Why: Finance ops need reproducible audit trails. LLMs hallucinate matches; a confidence threshold plus reason codes keeps unresolved work visible instead of “fixed” in silence. Trade off: Residual judgment quality depends on OPENAI API KEY . Without it, HeuristicJudge + n gram still run the audited batch unchanged. 2. Split harness/ from the Next.js app Decision: Accuracy critical code lives in a framework free package ( controller harness via file:../harness ). The app is thin API + UI + ops. Why: Vitest runs without Next, Prisma, or React. CI can gate the engine independently. Dashboard churn cannot silently break settlement math. Trade off: Deploy must include the sibling harness/ folder (see DEPLOYMENT.md ). 3. Integer paise, never floats Decision: All money amounts are signed integers (paise). Why: Avoid IEEE rounding in netting identity gross − fee − tax on fee − refund + adjustment = settlement . 4. Honest exceptions over inflated match rate Decision: Every unresolved record gets a ReasonCode + rationale + expected/actual split. Exception list integrity is tested; empty because hidden fails the bar. Why: One cherry picked match proves nothing. The demo sells trust, not 100% fantasy resolve. 5. Graceful degradation for Redis / OpenAI / Razorpay Decision: Optional services are no ops when unset. Local npm run dev / npm test / npm run batch stay green with an empty env. Why: Hackathon and reviewer machines should not require Upstash or API keys to see the loop. 6. BullMQ + LangGraph only when REDIS URL is set Decision: Same close graph runs in process or as a queued worker. Why: Demo path needs zero infra; production path needs durable checkpoints and horizontal workers without forking the engine. 7. Ground truth labeled synthetic batch Decision: Fixed seed 81 record batch across four sources with labels for precision/recall. Why: Match rate is measured, not assumed. Adversarial + invariant tests lock conservation laws (partition, netting identity, no bare fuzzy merges). 8. Prisma / Supabase optional Decision: Schema mirrors harness types, but the close loop works from Redis/in memory stores for the demo. Why: Persistence is valuable; it is not on the critical path for proving reconciliation math. 9. Razorpay test mode + webhooks as adapters Decision: Live sync and HMAC webhooks are opt in; CSV upload and the synthetic batch remain first class. Why: Real formats without forcing live money or fragile demo credentials. 10. Co located dashboard screens Decision: Follow app/AGENTS.md — page + components/ + sidebar registration. Why: Keeps UI consistent with the shared admin shell used across related hackathon tracks.","href":"/engineering/decisions","path":"engineering/decisions.mdx"},{"title":"Roadmap","description":"Prioritized backlog beyond the hackathon-complete close loop (P0–P3) and explicit non-goals.","headings":["P0 — Trust & production readiness","P1 — Accuracy & coverage","P2 — Product surface","P3 — Scale & cost","Explicit non-goals (for now)"],"text":"Prioritized backlog beyond the hackathon complete close loop (phases 0–6 in BUILD PLAN.md ). P0 — Trust & production readiness Item Why Multi tenant org isolation on every close API Prevent cross merchant run/exception leakage Role gates enforced server side ( owner / accountant / viewer ) on resolve/finalize UI only RBAC is not enough Signed export of CloseReport (hash + actor + timestamp) Audit package for finance sign off Webhook idempotency ledger for Razorpay events Duplicate payment.captured must not double ingest P1 — Accuracy & coverage Item Why Real bank statement parsers (CSV/MT940/CAMT) Beyond synthetic UTR shapes Configurable fee schedules per MID / method Netting without planting FEE rows Chargeback / dispute legs in the same close Completes the money lifecycle Per entity FX books (extend fx.ts ) Multi currency legal entities Human in the loop resolve UX with suggested splits Faster exception clearance P2 — Product surface Item Why Scheduled daily close (cron → enqueue close runs ) Hands off ops Slack / email digest of open exceptions Bring work to accountants Diff view: run N vs run N−1 Spot regression in match rate Read only “board” dashboard (match %, exception aging) Exec glance without cockpit noise CSV template download + column mapper Self serve onboarding P3 — Scale & cost Item Why Shard large uploads (10k+ rows) with progress events Keep UI live under load Cache deterministic match indexes per source day Cut re close latency Bound / batch residual LLM calls with prompt caching Cost control at volume Worker autoscaling policy docs Ops runbooks for Redis + BullMQ Explicit non goals (for now) Full double entry GL / journal posting GST filing submission Multi PSP abstraction beyond Razorpay adapters Billing / SaaS metering for ReconAI itself When picking the next slice, prefer anything that raises measured trust (isolation, audit, idempotency) before cosmetic dashboard work.","href":"/engineering/roadmap","path":"engineering/roadmap.mdx"},{"title":"Tech Stack","description":"What ReconAI uses end-to-end — harness, Next.js app, LLM, ops, auth, and what stays optional.","headings":["Layers","Where the LLM is used (and where it is not)","Env knobs (optional = demo still works)","Repo layout","Related"],"text":"ReconAI splits accuracy critical engine code ( harness/ ) from a thin Next.js surface ( app/ ). Optional services degrade gracefully so local demo and CI stay green with an empty env. Layers Layer Choice Role Core engine TypeScript in harness/ — zero runtime deps Matching, netting, settle, forecast, tax, exceptions, close Tests / CLI Vitest · batch · benchmark · gen batch · agent Measured baseline, coverage gate, headless runs App framework Next.js App Router · React · TypeScript strict Close Cockpit UI + REST API UI Tailwind · shadcn/ui · recharts · tanstack table Grids, KPI charts, exception drawers Agent / residual LLM OpenAI ( OPENAI API KEY ) via residual judge + settlement chat Residual flaps + narration only Orchestration LangGraph StateGraph · optional RedisSaver Close stage order + revision loop Queue BullMQ + npm run worker when REDIS URL set Durable close runs; else in process Cache / rate limit Upstash Redis REST (optional) Run store + rate limiting Auth Supabase Auth ( owner / accountant / viewer ) Session + role gates Persistence Prisma + Postgres (optional) Mirrors harness types when configured Payments adapter Razorpay test mode + HMAC webhooks (optional) Live sync; CSV / synthetic remain first class Where the LLM is used (and where it is not) Path Uses LLM? Notes Exact / normalized / netting match No Pure rules + paise identity Residual flaps without OPENAI API KEY No HeuristicJudge + n gram semantic Residual flaps with key Yes OpenAI residual judge → may emit AI RESOLVED Settlement Q&A Yes (optional) Streams cited answers; deterministic fallback if no key Tax category residual Maybe Rules first; judge fallback for ambiguous descriptions Fee / tax / settlement amounts Never Always from ingested records via FinanceCore Match rate / precision / recall Never Computed from labels + engine outcomes Philosophy: LLM everywhere is the trap. The model arbitrates residual ambiguity and narrates; it does not fudge numbers. See Engineering Decisions. Env knobs (optional = demo still works) Variable Enables Without it OPENAI API KEY Residual LLM judge, chat, embeddings HeuristicJudge + n gram REDIS URL BullMQ queue + durable checkpoints In process close Supabase URL / keys Auth + Postgres Local / in memory demo path Razorpay keys Sync + payment links + webhooks CSV upload + synthetic batch Full tables: Deployment · Local Dev. Repo layout Related Track 04 — brief ↔ product ↔ use mapping Architecture — system shape + pipeline FinanceCore — modules and judge modes API Overview — route map","href":"/engineering/stack","path":"engineering/stack.mdx"},{"title":"2-Minute Demo","description":"Honesty-first walkthrough: measured batch numbers, Close Cockpit, exceptions, and grounded forecast.","headings":["The honesty moment","Script (≈2 minutes)","1. Measured batch (not a slide)","2. Close Cockpit","3. Run Detail","4. Exception List","5. Settlement Q&A + Forecast","Talking points"],"text":"ReconAI demos the finance close the way a controller actually works — deterministic matches first, explicit residuals, and an honest exception list. Nothing is silently dropped. The honesty moment Matches are reproducible. Residuals get confidence + reason . Anything below threshold is filed with a reason code — never silently dropped: Reason code Meaning NO KEY No join key across sources AMOUNT MISMATCH Amounts do not reconcile PARTIAL FLAP Partial / flap match DATE SKEW Date window mismatch LOW CONFIDENCE Residual below confidence threshold DUPLICATE Duplicate candidate Script (≈2 minutes) 1. Measured batch (not a slide) Show the locked baseline: Precision and recall are grounded in labels — measured, not assumed. 2. Close Cockpit Open /dashboard/close . Start a run. KPIs climb as the engine reconciles payments, settlements, and invoices. 3. Run Detail Open /dashboard/close/[runId] : Match rate bars and confidence distribution Reconciliation grid Click a match → why chip (e.g. exact:utr , conf 0.99 ) 4. Exception List Open /dashboard/close/exceptions : Reason codes + rationale on every open line Agent can file LOW CONFIDENCE live Resolve / override is audited — exceptions are never deleted 5. Settlement Q&A + Forecast Settlement ( /dashboard/close/settlement ) — cited answers over matched records Forecast ( /dashboard/close/forecast ) — 7 day cash band grounded in matched settlement lags Talking points Pillar One liner FinanceCore chokepoint One audited funnel; rules first, model only for residual Deterministic first Reproducible matches; confidence + reason everywhere Measured, not assumed Ground truth labels → match rate, precision, recall Honest exceptions Structured reason codes; zero silent drops Graceful ops Redis / OpenAI / Razorpay optional; in process fallback","href":"/guides/demo-script","path":"guides/demo-script.mdx"},{"title":"Deployment","description":"Deploy ReconAI locally or on Vercel, with optional Redis workers and production checklist.","headings":["Prerequisites","Local development","core engine (tests + batch)","dashboard + API","Environment variables","Database (optional)","set DATABASE_URL in .env.local","or apply SQL under supabase/","Vercel (recommended for the web app)","Smoke checks after deploy","Durable worker (production)","CI","Production checklist"],"text":"Deploy the Next.js dashboard ( app/ ) and optionally a durable BullMQ worker. The deterministic harness in harness/ has no runtime deps and is linked into the app as controller harness ( file:../harness ). Prerequisites Node.js 20+ npm 10+ Optional: Supabase (Postgres + Auth), Upstash Redis, OpenAI, Razorpay test keys Local demo works with an empty .env.local — the engine falls back to in memory / HeuristicJudge. Local development Optional durable worker (requires REDIS URL ): Environment variables Copy from app/.env.example . Summary: Variable Required for If unset NEXT PUBLIC SUPABASE URL / NEXT PUBLIC SUPABASE ANON KEY Auth + persisted app data Seed / in memory paths DATABASE URL Prisma → Postgres Skip DB; demo store UPSTASH REDIS REST URL / UPSTASH REDIS REST TOKEN Run store, rate limit, cache No ops REDIS URL BullMQ queue + LangGraph checkpointer + npm run worker In process close runs OPENAI API KEY Residual LLM judge, settlement chat, embeddings HeuristicJudge + n gram RAZORPAY KEY ID / RAZORPAY KEY SECRET Live test sync CSV / 81 record batch RAZORPAY WEBHOOK SECRET POST /api/webhooks/razorpay HMAC Unsigned webhooks rejected Never prefix Razorpay secrets with NEXT PUBLIC . Database (optional) Schema lives in prisma/schema.prisma and mirrors harness/src/core/types.ts . Vercel (recommended for the web app) 1. Import https://github.com/Rhae Shane/ReconAI . 2. Root Directory: app . 3. Enable Include source files outside of the Root Directory in the Build Step so file:../harness resolves. 4. Framework Preset: Next.js. Build: npm run build . Install: npm install . 5. Add env vars from the table above in Project Settings → Environment Variables. 6. Deploy. Webhook URL for Razorpay (test mode): Events: payment.captured , refund.processed , settlement.processed . Smoke checks after deploy GET /api/health → { service: \"reconai\", ... } Open / → landing; /dashboard/close → Close Cockpit Upload CSV via Close flow or start the seeded batch run Durable worker (production) Vercel serverless is fine for the UI/API without REDIS URL (synchronous in process closes). For queued / durable closes: 1. Provision Upstash Redis; set both REST vars and REDIS URL (TCP / ioredis URI). 2. Run the worker on a long lived host (Railway, Fly.io, Render, a VM): 3. Scale workers horizontally; BullMQ + RedisSaver keep run state shared. CI GitHub Actions ( .github/workflows/ci.yml ) runs: 1. harness — install, test 2. app — install, lint, typecheck, unit tests, ops verify, production build Production checklist [ ] No secrets in the repo ( .env ignored; only .env.example committed) [ ] Razorpay keys are test mode until go live review [ ] Webhook secret matches Dashboard → Webhooks [ ] OPENAI API KEY present if you want live residual judgment / chat [ ] Redis + worker only if you need durable queues at scale [ ] npm run batch / harness tests green on the release commit","href":"/guides/deployment","path":"guides/deployment.mdx"},{"title":"Local Development","description":"Run the ReconAI harness and Next.js app locally — scripts, optional Prisma, empty-env fallbacks.","headings":["Quick start","core — fully testable with empty env","dashboard","Harness scripts","App scripts","Optional Prisma","set DATABASE_URL in .env.local","or apply SQL under supabase/","Empty env works"],"text":"ReconAI is two packages: a framework agnostic harness/ engine and the app/ app (thin API + UI + worker). An empty .env.local is enough for the demo — Redis, OpenAI, Razorpay, and Postgres are all optional. Quick start Expected batch shape (labeled synthetic set, locked by tests): Harness scripts Run from harness/ : Script Command What it does Tests npm test Vitest unit + integration suite Coverage npm run test:cov Vitest with coverage gate Batch npm run batch Run the labeled 81 record close; print measured summary Gen batch npm run gen batch Generate a synthetic batch fixture Agent npm run agent CLI agent driver over close tools Bench npm run bench Throughput / timing benchmark The harness has zero runtime dependencies . It is consumed by the app as controller harness via file:../harness . App scripts Run from app/ : Script Command What it does Dev npm run dev Next.js on port 3000 (Turbopack) Build npm run build Production Next.js build Worker npm run worker BullMQ consumer (idle safe without REDIS URL ; consumes when set) Ops verify npm run verify:ops Honesty / ops smoke checks used in CI Related: npm run verify:reconcile for reconcile path verification; npm test for app unit tests. Optional Prisma Durable Postgres is optional. When you want it: Schema: prisma/schema.prisma (mirrors harness/src/core/types.ts ). Empty env works Layer Without credentials Close runs In process synchronous path (no BullMQ) Judge / chat HeuristicJudge + n gram similarity Run store In memory demo store Razorpay CSV upload + seeded 81 record batch Auth / DB Seed / demo paths See Deployment for the full env table and Vercel setup.","href":"/guides/local-dev","path":"guides/local-dev.mdx"},{"title":"Razorpay Integration","description":"Test keys, sync API, webhooks (payment.captured, refund.processed, settlement.processed), and HMAC verification.","headings":["Test keys","app/.env.local","Sync — pull + flush inbox","Webhooks — HMAC-verified ingest","Events to subscribe","Signature verification","Razorpay sends:","Header: X-Razorpay-Signature: <hmac>","Body:   JSON event payload","Production notes"],"text":"When Razorpay is unset, the close loop stays on CSV upload and the synthetic 81 record batch. With test mode keys, you can pull live payments/settlements/refunds and ingest Dashboard webhooks into the close inbox. Test keys From Razorpay Dashboard → API Keys (Test mode) and Webhooks . Set server only env vars in .env.local (never NEXT PUBLIC ): Variable Purpose RAZORPAY KEY ID Test key id ( rzp test ... ) RAZORPAY KEY SECRET Test key secret RAZORPAY WEBHOOK SECRET HMAC secret for webhook signature verification GET /api/health reports checks.razorpay: true when key id + secret are present. GET /api/close/razorpay/sync returns { configured, inbox, mode } without leaking secrets ( mode is test / live / unknown ). Sync — pull + flush inbox Pulls payments, settlements, and refunds from Razorpay (when configured) and flushes the webhook inbox into a close run. Requires owner or accountant . Outcome Status Meaning Success 201 Close run created; body includes runId , counts , mode Unconfigured 503 Missing RAZORPAY KEY ID / RAZORPAY KEY SECRET Empty 400 No payments, settlements, refunds, or inbox rows to reconcile You can also trigger sync from the Close Cockpit Razorpay card at /dashboard/close . Webhooks — HMAC verified ingest Point Razorpay Dashboard → Webhooks (test mode) at: Events to subscribe Event Mapped into close inbox payment.captured Payment records refund.processed Refund records settlement.processed Settlement records Signature verification The handler reads the raw body and verifies X Razorpay Signature against RAZORPAY WEBHOOK SECRET (HMAC). Invalid signatures return 401 { error: \"invalid signature\" } . Successful ingest returns: Webhook rows sit in the inbox until you flush them with POST /api/close/razorpay/sync . Production notes Keep keys in test mode until go live review (see Deployment checklist). Webhook secret in env must match Dashboard → Webhooks. Unsigned or wrong secret requests are rejected — there is no “skip HMAC” path when a secret is configured.","href":"/guides/razorpay-integration","path":"guides/razorpay-integration.mdx"},{"title":"Quickstart","description":"Run the ReconAI harness batch and open the Close Cockpit in under 2 minutes.","headings":["Prerequisites","1. Run the harness","2. Start the dashboard","3. Optional durable worker","2-minute demo","UI map","Next"],"text":"Prerequisites Node.js 20+ npm 10+ Local demo works with an empty .env.local — the engine falls back to in memory storage and HeuristicJudge . 1. Run the harness Framework agnostic core — no runtime deps, fully testable with empty env: Expected batch output (labeled synthetic set, locked by tests): Use npm run test:cov when you need the coverage gate. 2. Start the dashboard Open http://localhost:3000. Supabase, Redis, OpenAI, and Razorpay keys are optional. Fill only what you need in .env.local . 3. Optional durable worker Default close runs execute in process (zero infra). With REDIS URL set, start the BullMQ worker: The worker is idle safe without REDIS URL ; it consumes the close runs queue when Redis is configured. See Deployment for the full env table. 2 minute demo 1. Harness — npm run batch in harness/ shows real measured numbers, not a slide. 2. Close Cockpit ( /dashboard/close ) — start a run; KPIs climb. 3. Run Detail ( /dashboard/close/[runId] ) — match rate bars, confidence distribution, reconciliation grid. Click a match for the why chip (e.g. exact:utr , conf 0.99 ). 4. Exception List ( /dashboard/close/exceptions ) — reason codes + rationale; residuals stay visible with confidence. 5. Settlement Q&A + Forecast ( /dashboard/close/settlement , /dashboard/close/forecast ) — cited answers; 7 day cash band grounded in matched lags. UI map Screen Route Close Cockpit /dashboard/close Run Detail /dashboard/close/[runId] Exceptions /dashboard/close/exceptions Settlement Q&A /dashboard/close/settlement Forecast /dashboard/close/forecast Tax /dashboard/close/tax Next Authentication & roles — Supabase auth and owner / accountant / viewer How It Works — FinanceCore pipeline Deployment — Vercel, Redis, and production env","href":"/quickstart","path":"quickstart.mdx"},{"title":"Track 04 — AI Finance Controller","description":"How ReconAI maps the hackathon brief — product, tech, and operator use — from why-now through the measured close bar.","headings":["The brief","Product side — what we sell","Why this wins","Example directions → product surfaces","The bar — three deliverables","Tech side — how we solve it","Architecture in one picture","Deterministic-first, LLM last","Stack (summary)","Use side — how an operator runs the loop","2-minute path","Operator map","Challenge checklist"],"text":"The brief Track: AI Finance Controller · Run the books and the cash position Build an agent that closes one finance ops loop across a 50+ record batch of synthetic data, reporting its match rate and the exceptions it could not resolve . Brief line ReconAI answer Why now Verification capacity — not generation speed — is the bottleneck. Reconciliation, settlement, and forecasting are still done by hand. Example directions Multi source reconciliation · Settlement Q&A agent · Forward cash forecaster · Tax line matcher — all four , in one close loop The bar Throughput + measured accuracy + an honest exception list. One cherry picked match proves nothing. Locked baseline (81 records, 4 sources — exceeds the 50+ bar): Product side — what we sell Why this wins 1. Exact “why now”. Matching one payment across gateway, bank UTR, ERP, and GST is pure verification work. ReconAI automates that loop with an auditable trail. 2. The bar is engineered in. Deterministic matching first → residual judge → confidence + reason on every decision → published match rate / precision / recall → structured exceptions. Nothing hidden. 3. Full loop, not a toy match. Ingest → reconcile → settle Q&A → forecast cash → tax map → close report. One narrative from messy batch to signed off books. 4. Trustworthy by design. The LLM never invents settlement math. FinanceCore records provenance; unresolved work is a first class artifact. Example directions → product surfaces Brief direction Product surface Where Multi source reconciliation Exact → normalized → netting → residual judge across gateway / bank / ERP / GST ReconciliationEngine + Close Cockpit / Run Detail Settlement Q&A agent Cited chat over the settled ledger /dashboard/close/settlement · POST /api/close/agents/chat Forward cash forecaster 7 day cash band from matched settlement lags /dashboard/close/forecast · CashForecaster Tax line matcher HSN / category rules + judge fallback /dashboard/close/tax · TaxMatcher The bar — three deliverables Deliverable Meaning Evidence Throughput Full audited batch well under a second; queue scales to thousands npm run batch · npm run benchmark · BullMQ worker Measured accuracy Match rate + precision / recall vs ground truth labels CloseReport · harness tests lock the baseline Honest exceptions Explicit matched / partial / unresolved + per record reason codes Exception List UI · ExceptionLedger · never silent drops Tech side — how we solve it Architecture in one picture Deterministic first, LLM last Stage Who decides LLM? Exact / normalized key match Rules No Fee / refund / adjustment netting Paise identity math No Residual flaps HeuristicJudge (default) or OpenAI residual judge Only if key set Settlement amounts / fees Source records Never invented by the model Settlement Q&A narration OpenAI stream or deterministic fallback Narrates engine facts Tax residual descriptions Rules first, judge fallback Residual only Rule: every agent tool / API / CLI call routes through FinanceCore. The model does not compute gross − fee − tax − refund + adjustment . Stack (summary) Layer Choice Core Framework free TypeScript in harness/ (Vitest gated) App Next.js App Router · React · Tailwind · shadcn/ui Agent / residual LLM OpenAI via app judge + settlement chat ( OPENAI API KEY optional) Orchestration LangGraph close graph; BullMQ when REDIS URL set Auth / data Supabase Auth + optional Prisma/Postgres Integrations Razorpay test sync + HMAC webhooks (optional) Full detail: Tech Stack. Pipeline depth: How It Works · FinanceCore · Architecture. Use side — how an operator runs the loop 2 minute path 1. cd harness && npm run batch — show measured numbers (not a slide). 2. Open /dashboard/close — start a run; KPIs climb. 3. Run Detail — match rate bars, why chips ( exact:utr , conf 0.99 ). 4. Exceptions — reason codes + rationale still visible. 5. Settlement Q&A + Forecast — cited answers; lag grounded cash band. Operator map Job Screen Start / upload / sync Close Cockpit Inspect matches Run ","href":"/track-04","path":"track-04.mdx"}]};
